#text("Measured on public synthetic prime-field workloads, 2026-10-14 UTC. Classification: accounting and boundary control. Follow-up to PR #1724 (https://github.com/aburan28/crypto/pull/1724).")
#parbreak()
#text("The existing MITM IC and matched negation-rho implementations are measured in Callgrind simulated user-space instructions over the complete methods::solve call. The interval includes cold setup inside the adapter, queries, relation handling, elimination, recovery and internal verification. It excludes input loading, method resolution, known-answer target construction, process launch, kernel instructions and the external independent point check. These exclusions remain unmeasured; they are not charged zero. No native wall-time speedup is claimed.")
#parbreak()
#text("Profiles verified against the archived scalars, points and deterministic phase counters: 100/100. The 32 archived workloads remain separate one-target solves. No setup or target transport is shared. The original eight samples per fixed curve are reused; this is accounting on those same points, not a fresh-target replication.")
#parbreak()
#text(size: 7.5pt)[#table(columns: 3, inset: 4pt, text("Gap"), text("IC floor/crater Ir"), text("99% interval"), text("ell8209-q29"), text("0.9688066"), text("0.5735211 to 1.492155"), text("ell131101-q37"), text("1.162501"), text("0.9016566 to 1.462762"))]
#parbreak()
#text("Frozen repeated instruction-lead criterion: not met. A/A within the frozen 2% gate: true. Maximum absolute relative deviation: 0.00002237726 (fraction). Intervals including one are not equivalence proofs. The estimates are implementation observations on two fixed pairs and cannot establish a conductor effect across isogeny classes.")
#parbreak()
#text("Comparison status: admissible_implementation_diagnostic. A failed A/A gate makes the instruction comparisons exploratory; failed or missing profiles make inference inadmissible.")
#parbreak()
#text(size: 7.5pt)[#table(columns: 3, inset: 4pt, text("ICV1 model"), text("IC / matched rho Ir"), text("Paired 99% interval"), text("icv1-fp29-t47-14392892"), text("28.15254"), text("14.01229 to 74.39444"), text("icv1-fp29-t47-1f934956"), text("25.27633"), text("13.30118 to 48.24704"), text("icv1-fp37-t277-91fd6e29"), text("47.77148"), text("34.84198 to 79.65082"), text("icv1-fp37-t277-090dc414"), text("47.07830"), text("29.44940 to 104.8381"))]
#parbreak()
#text("These ratios compare the same one-target workloads within the frozen instruction interval; excluded work and native wall time remain unmeasured.")
